416
00:32:50,640 --> 00:32:54,640
Salmon is king catch in America's Pacific Northwest.

417
00:32:54,641 --> 00:32:57,240
Northwest.

418
00:32:57,241 --> 00:33:02,860
Every year, over two million pounds of its pink flesh are pulled out of the Columbia River.

419
00:33:02,861 --> 00:33:11,780
But 10,000 years before modern canneries and fishing boats first materialized, Native American

420
00:33:11,781 --> 00:33:17,140
tribes in the region were trapping salmon along the Columbia's banks.

421
00:33:17,141 --> 00:33:23,600
Since the beginning of time, our people have been fishing here.

422
00:33:23,601 --> 00:33:29,840
All these scaffolds here are handed down from one generation to the next.

423
00:33:29,841 --> 00:33:36,600
This site, Lyle Falls, is located on the Klickitat River, one of the last undammed tributaries

424
00:33:36,601 --> 00:33:40,540
of the Columbia in south central Washington.

425
00:33:40,541 --> 00:33:44,240
For thousands of years, the tribes here have practiced a traditional method of trapping

426
00:33:44,241 --> 00:33:48,080
salmon called dip netting.

427
00:33:48,081 --> 00:33:52,280
This pole is about 35 feet long.

428
00:33:52,281 --> 00:33:56,120
And I'll push it down until I hit the bottom.

429
00:33:56,121 --> 00:34:00,920
Let the net drift along the bottom without trying to hit the bottom.

430
00:34:00,921 --> 00:34:06,140
Because the vibration off the hoop will send it to the fish and the fish will see the hoop.

431
00:34:06,141 --> 00:34:13,560
The way we catch these fish with these hoops, nets, is generally by feel.

432
00:34:13,561 --> 00:34:17,760
The pole is like an extension of you.

433
00:34:17,761 --> 00:34:18,600
You can feel them.

434
00:34:20,480 --> 00:34:22,520
If a fish swims into the dip net,

435
00:34:22,521 --> 00:34:24,020
the net collapses around it.

436
00:34:26,420 --> 00:34:28,280
The fishermen must then yank up the net

437
00:34:28,281 --> 00:34:29,860
before the fish gets loose.

438
00:34:31,640 --> 00:34:32,480
Ah, dang it.

439
00:34:34,380 --> 00:34:36,340
I didn't feel that when he got away.

440
00:34:39,200 --> 00:34:40,240
Felt him too late.

441
00:34:41,960 --> 00:34:44,380
But James Keona's Yakima and other tribes

442
00:34:44,381 --> 00:34:46,420
may not be dip netting here much longer.

443
00:34:46,421 --> 00:35:00,053
Overfishing from 1866 to the 1930s and the introduction of hydroelectric dams in 1932 have pushed the wild-born salmon population below one million fish, less than 10%

444
00:35:00,054 --> 00:35:02,420
of its numbers 200 years ago.

445
00:35:02,421 --> 00:35:16,421
To ensure the salmon remain a sustainable resource, the Yakima, Warm Springs, Nez Perce, and Umatilla tribes formed the Columbia River Intertribal Fish Commission, or

446
00:35:17,841 --> 00:35:19,420
CRITVIC, in 1977.

447
00:35:19,421 --> 00:35:26,420
CRITVIC researchers use various traps to study the salmon population.

448
00:35:26,421 --> 00:35:33,380
and one of them is integrated into the fish ladder, or fish pass, at Bonneville Dam.

449
00:35:35,320 --> 00:35:39,340
The tramp monitors adult salmon swimming back upstream from the ocean

450
00:35:39,341 --> 00:35:41,640
as they make their way to their natal streams.

451
00:35:42,820 --> 00:35:46,740
We sample the sockeye as well as chinook and steelhead

452
00:35:46,741 --> 00:35:50,680
to get length measurements, to collect scales

453
00:35:50,681 --> 00:35:52,940
from which we can determine the age of the fish,

454
00:35:53,300 --> 00:35:56,220
and we also put small tags in the fish.

455
00:35:56,420 --> 00:35:59,780
that we then contract the fish as they go upstream.

456
00:36:00,920 --> 00:36:04,520
When they hit the dam, the fish are diverted into the mouth of the ladder.

457
00:36:07,340 --> 00:36:11,820
Salmon instinctively swim against the current, so the trap simulates that condition.

458
00:36:13,160 --> 00:36:17,160
The fish swim past gates in the ladder until they reach a holding tank.

459
00:36:19,660 --> 00:36:24,880
When workers shut the tank's gates, they activate water jets to simulate the current.

460
00:36:25,880 --> 00:36:29,240
The fish swim up over the jets and onto a water slide.

461
00:36:31,440 --> 00:36:34,340
A technician diverts the salmon to the research tank,

462
00:36:34,600 --> 00:36:36,920
but lets the other fish pass through the system,

